# Self-hosting

Clone the repository and install dependencies in the environment that will build the web application:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Uncoil-dev/Uncoil
cd Uncoil
npm ci
npm run build
```

Uncoil runs on four services. Set each one up and put its settings in server-side environment variables:

| Service | What it stores or does | Settings |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Convex | App data: projects, run summaries, alerts and comments | `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL` |
| ClickHouse | Raw spans and time-series telemetry | `CLICKHOUSE_URL`, `CLICKHOUSE_USER`, `CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD` |
| Inngest | Background jobs that move ingested spans into ClickHouse and Convex | `INNGEST_EVENT_KEY`, `INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY` |
| Redis | Cache between ClickHouse and the dashboard | `REDIS_URL` |

Add your authentication settings and provider keys the same way. Use separate Convex, ClickHouse, Inngest and Redis environments for staging and production, and verify authentication before exposing dashboard routes.
